From cae01b9873adee12c85147c33d71e231f34508f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Villar <15879262+nvillar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:58:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Duo: three-finger gesture recognizer, logging only

Prototype of the Surface Duo three-finger app gestures (docs/dual-screen-plan.md, three-finger gesture
decision): it recognises them and logs what it recognised, and takes no action. Actions (span, contract,
move/swap) come later, on top of the topology controller and the move/span commands.

| Gesture | Logged as |
|---|---|
| pinch-out, three fingers on one panel | gesture=SPAN target=<that panel> |
| pinch-in, three fingers on one panel | gesture=CONTRACT target=<that panel> |
| pinch with fingers on both panels | out = SPAN, in = CONTRACT; target = panel with two of the three |
| sideways swipe on one panel toward the other | gesture=PUSH target=<from> to=<other> |

DuoThreeFingerClassifier (pure Java on DuoPanelGeometry, no Android dependencies) classifies fingers by
the panel they land on and decides once, when the spread change reaches 40 dp or the translation 80 dp:
the winner must beat the other measure 2:1 (across the panels the pinch must be at least half the
translation across the hinge, and swipes with fingers on both panels are cancelled), every finger must
agree with it, and a push must be across the hinge (not along it) and toward the other panel. Otherwise
the gesture is cancelled with a reason. Fingers may start moving while the others land (300 ms), and are
measured from where they landed. Touches starting in an edge-swipe zone (outer edges and hinge-side
edges 24 dp, top 32 dp, bottom 48 dp) are ineligible; contacts on the hinge band or the display boundary
(controller artefacts, fingers parked after sliding off an edge) are ignored, and a finger reaching the
boundary counts as lifted. A recognised gesture is followed to the first lift and reported as COMMIT, or as
CANCEL reversed if it went back below half its threshold. Works for every rotation (the axis is the one
across the hinge) and needs both panels on the display (spanned or gapless).

DuoThreeFingerGestureMonitor (CoreStartable, DuoGestureModule in ReferenceSystemUIModule) feeds it
from a gesture input monitor on the default display. It never pilfers pointers, so input delivery is
unchanged. Off by default; runs only on a Duo with sys.duode.panels.active=1 and
`settings put global duode_three_finger_gestures 1`; `duode_three_finger_gestures_config` overrides
thresholds (for example "pinchDp=30,swipeDp=60"); both apply without a restart. Touches starting on the
keyguard and touches with a stylus are reported as cancelled. One log line per result, tag DuoGesture:

  event=RECOGNIZED gesture=SPAN motion=pinch-out split=3+0 target=0 to=-1 pinchPx=+108 scale=1.60
  acrossPx=+9 alongPx=-20 ms=1040 rot=0 reason=pinch

dumpsys activity service com.android.systemui/.SystemUIService
com.android.systemui.duo.gesture.DuoThreeFingerGestureMonitor shows the state and the last 20 results.

Host tests: DuoThreeFingerClassifierTests (java_test_host, 35 cases on synthetic touch streams: every
gesture, rotations 1-3, gapless, edge zones, fourth finger, bounce, reversal, keyguard, single panel).
The DUO-DE harness also replays raw getevent captures from a Duo 1 through the classifier
(tools/duo-gesture). Not built in an Android tree or run on a device yet; the SystemUI classes were
type-checked against the r4 SystemUI-core and framework header jars, without Dagger processing.

Co-authored-by: Copilot App <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
